I see this:
```
matt@participant2:~$ mysqlctld
E1023 15:17:35.702790   47552 metrics_cgroup.go:57] Failed to init cgroup1 manager: failed to load cgroup1: cgroups: cgroup mountpoint does not exist
panic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference
[signal SIGSEGV: segmentation violation code=0x1 addr=0x68 pc=0x1422f20]

goroutine 1 [running]:
vitess.io/vitess/go/vt/servenv.getCgroup1CpuUsage()
        vitess.io/vitess/go/vt/servenv/metrics_cgroup.go:126 +0x20
vitess.io/vitess/go/vt/servenv.init.8()
        vitess.io/vitess/go/vt/servenv/metrics_cgroup.go:60 +0xd8
```

That error is coming from here: https://github.com/containerd/cgroups/blob/bce3c7e5fbf05852294998684293918fcb3f59dd/cgroup1/v1.go#L47-L73

@reporter I'm not sure if you'd get this same error though as I would expect the mount point to be there. So it may have been a different error in your case. 

This clearly demonstrates the general problem in that we do not handle failures here and panic. But I'm not sure if we should just remove v1 support, or tweak things more so that it doesn't fail at all in your case.

@reporter I'm assuming you have Debian 10 machines available. Is there any chance that you can build Vitess from main after applying this patch and then `mysqlctld`? It's really this part that we care about here:
```
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ func getCgroup1() (cgroup1.Cgroup, error) {
        path := cgroup1.NestedPath("")
        cgroup, err := cgroup1.Load(path)
        if err != nil {
-               return nil, fmt.Errorf("cgroup1 manager is nil")
+               return nil, fmt.Errorf("failed to load cgroup1: %v", err)
        }
        return cgroup, nil
 }
```

So that we can see the actual error that is returned in your case. Or if you can at least run this within a pod in your k8s cluster:
```
mount | grep cgroup
```

For now I will go forward with addressing the error/failure handling.
